Mathematical result
-------------------
Starting equation and established notation:
z^2 Psi''+(B1+B2 z)Psi'+(B3+q z)Psi=0, q != 0,
B1=2 conjugate(F)/V, B2=2 hbar omega0/V, B3=-2E/V, q=2F/V.

For z=t^2 and Y(t)=Psi(t^2), direct chain rule gives exactly
Y''+[(2B2-1)/t+2B1/t^3]Y'+[4q+4B3/t^2]Y=0.

With s^2=-q, lambda_sigma=2 sigma s, and c0=1, the formal ansatz is
Y_sigma=exp(lambda_sigma t)t^rho sum_{n>=0} c_n^(sigma)t^(-n).
The characteristic and power equations are
lambda_sigma^2+4q=0 and lambda_sigma(2rho+2B2-1)=0, hence
lambda_sigma=2 sigma s and rho=1/2-B2.

Locally writing A=2B2-1, C=2B1, D=4B3, the recurrence is
2 lambda_sigma n c_n =
[(rho-n+1)(rho-n)+A(rho-n+1)+D]c_{n-1}
+ lambda_sigma C c_{n-2}+C(rho-n+3)c_{n-3}, n>=1,
with c_{-1}=c_{-2}=0.

In the manuscript's compact notation
K=rho^2+(2B2-2)rho+4B3 (called C there), the first terms are
c1=K/(2 lambda),
c2=B1/2+K(K+2)/(8 lambda^2),
c3=K(K+2)(K+6)/(48 lambda^3)
   +B1(3K+6+4rho)/(12 lambda).
After truncation at c3 the normalized-equation residual first occurs at
t^(-5); in the equivalent equation multiplied by t^2 it first occurs at
t^(-3), and this coefficient determines c4.

For a half-turn with Log(-t)=Log(t)+epsilon i pi, epsilon=+1 or -1,
c_n^(-sigma)=(-1)^n c_n^(sigma) and the exact normalized formal relation is
Y_sigma(-t)=exp(epsilon i pi rho)Y_{-sigma}(t).
The left side denotes continuation along the chosen half-turn. The phase is
generally essential. This agrees with the stage-07a/07b geometry because the
exponentials exchange while Re(4st)=0 is equal-modulus and Im(4st)=0 is
constant-phase geometry.

